WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.250
This is the deck builder.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.730
You tell it what deck you need...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.450
and it builds it for you, from the approved template.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.330
So it's always on brand.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.070
Start with the brief.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.190
Say what the deck's for, who it's for, and how many slides you want.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.670
The more concrete you are, the better the deck.

00:00:17.081 --> 00:00:18.731
Then attach your material.

00:00:18.681 --> 00:00:22.931
A PDF, a Word or PowerPoint file, an Excel sheet...

00:00:22.761 --> 00:00:24.891
or just paste a link in the brief.

00:00:24.841 --> 00:00:28.451
The deck is written from it, and your brief decides the angle.

00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:33.113
If the deck needs an agenda and section dividers, turn on Chapters.

00:00:32.903 --> 00:00:35.593
If it runs straight through, just leave it off.

00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:37.695
Now press Generate.

00:00:37.685 --> 00:00:45.335
If your material leaves something open, like which sheet to use or what to headline, you'll get a few questions written for your files.

00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:46.815
Answer them, or skip.

00:00:47.431 --> 00:00:50.139
And the slides arrive, one by one.

00:00:50.169 --> 00:00:54.739
Charts use the numbers from your sheet, and the photos come from the Giga library.

00:00:56.394 --> 00:00:57.364
Need more?

00:00:57.354 --> 00:01:03.084
Generate more slides lets you describe what's missing, and the new slides land right where they belong.

00:01:02.874 --> 00:01:05.844
Or pick a layout yourself, with Add slide.

00:01:11.172 --> 00:01:13.142
To present, press play.

00:01:13.092 --> 00:01:16.302
It goes full screen, with the template's animations.

00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:19.582
Use the arrow keys to move, and Escape to leave.

00:01:23.843 --> 00:01:29.053
Finally, download the deck as a PDF, a PowerPoint, or HTML.

00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:32.813
Nothing is stored on a server, so keep that HTML file...

00:01:32.643 --> 00:01:35.293
you can upload it here again and keep editing.
